      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fort Fanning Historic Park sits on a strategic bend of the Suwannee River, overlooking Seminole chief Bolek’s Old Town across the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fanning_Springs%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fanning Springs is a junction on the Nature Coast State Trail, a rail‑trail that follows abandoned railway lines through North Central Florida.",
